## Conservation Diagnostics {#sec-conservation}

The two discrete conservation laws of interest are **Faraday's law**

$$\frac{\mathbf{B}^{n+1} - \mathbf{B}^n}{\Delta t} + \nabla\times\mathbf{E}^m = 0$$

and the **quasineutrality constraint** $\delta n_i \ll n_0$. The first is enforced exactly by construction of `apply_faraday!` (machine-precision residual at every step). The second is monitored via $\max_x|n_i(x,t) - 1|$, which should remain small in the linear regime and grow at most algebraically as nonlinear effects develop.

```julia; echo=false
# Helper: compute max spectral-curl residual ‖Bz^{n+1} − Bz^n + dt·(∇×E)_z‖∞ over time.
# For 1-D grids, (∇×E)_z = ∂_{x1} E_y  →  ik_{x1} Ê_y in Fourier space.
function faraday_residuals(diag, dt, grid)
    Nx = size(grid.xaxes[1], 1)
    k1 = fftfreq(Nx, 1/grid.delta[1]) .* 2π
    residuals = Float64[]
    for n in 2:length(diag.t)
        curlEz = real.(ifft(im .* k1 .* fft(diag.Ey[n-1])))
        R = diag.Bz[n] .- diag.Bz[n-1] .+ dt .* curlEz
        push!(residuals, maximum(abs.(R)))
    end
    return residuals
end

# Helper: max density deviation from background n₀=1.
qn_deviation(diag) = [maximum(abs.(ni .- 1.0)) for ni in diag.ni]
```

```julia; echo=false, label="fig-faraday-kin", fig_cap="Faraday residual ‖Bz^{n+1}−Bz^n+dt·∂_{x1}Ey‖∞ over time for all four kinetic simulations. Dashed line: machine ε. Zero by construction of apply_faraday!."

runs_kin = [
    ("Par β=$(βi_lo)",  diag_par_lo,  grid_par_kin),
    ("Par β=$(βi_hi)",  diag_par_hi,  grid_par_kin),
    ("Perp β=$(βi_lo)", diag_perp_lo, grid_perp_kin),
    ("Perp β=$(βi_hi)", diag_perp_hi, grid_perp_kin),
]

fig = Figure(size=(1000, 420))
ax = Axis(fig[1,1], xlabel="t / Ωᵢ⁻¹", ylabel="‖Faraday residual‖∞", yscale=log10,
          title="Faraday conservation")
for (ci, (label, diag, grid)) in enumerate(runs_kin)
    res = faraday_residuals(diag, dt_kin, grid)
    t_res = diag.t[2:end]
    lines!(ax, t_res, res; color=WONG[ci+1], label=label)
end
hlines!(ax, [eps(Float64)]; color=:gray, linestyle=:dash, label="machine ε")
axislegend(ax; position=:rt)
fig
```

```julia; echo=false, label="fig-qn-kin", fig_cap="Quasineutrality indicator max|nᵢ−1| over time for all four kinetic simulations. Small values confirm the linear regime; saturation marks nonlinear onset."

fig = Figure(size=(1000, 420))
ax = Axis(fig[1,1], xlabel="t / Ωᵢ⁻¹", ylabel="max|nᵢ − 1|", yscale=log10,
          title="Quasineutrality indicator")
for (ci, (label, diag, _)) in enumerate(runs_kin)
    dev = qn_deviation(diag)
    lines!(ax, diag.t, dev; color=WONG[ci+1], label=label)
end
axislegend(ax; position=:lt)
fig
```